	(text "Place 1uF near high side fets"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 277.876 134.874 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "7fba76a3-1dee-41ef-a702-d2bbd98ee852")
	)
	(text "Current Sense Discussion\n\nFor this esc setup, the motor driver ensures that VREF/2 is the middle reference point for the current sensing, where here VREF is 3V3.\nFrom here, a gain of 10 is selected, in order to provide the mcu with an idle voltage of 1.65V when there is no current flowing through \na phase. This means, that under peak load (22A), we can expect a max voltage (assuming 4m shunt) of:\n\nV_out = 1.65 +- (Gain * I * R_shunt\n	  = 1.65 +-  (10 *  22 * 0.004) \n      = 2.53V\n\nThis is below the maimum of 3V3, which is ideal. This is because we need some headroom to detect if ever there \nis an overcurrent event in one of the phases. If this was too close, it would either have false detections, or be hard to detect\nsuch an event.\n\nWe can also calculate the maximum power dissipated trough this shunt as follows\n\nP = I^2 * R_shunt\n  = (22)^2 * 0.04 \n  = 1.94 W"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 421.64 168.402 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a1c33899-5dc3-46e2-96ef-adf4747b4556")
	)
	(text "This capacitor bank is expected to handle a total ripple current of:\ni_c = 0.65 * I_phase_rms * 1.1\n    = 0.65 * 15.56 *1.1 \n	= 11.12A\n\nThe total amount of capacitance required for full load would be:\nC = i_c /(delta_V * f_sw).\nGiven a 10% maximum allowable voltage ripple on the DC Bus, the require capacitance is:\nC = 11.12 / (2.4 * 25k)\n  = 185uF\n\nTaking a 10uF capacitor, we will need 18 caps.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 58.928 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ac2aef24-abd5-438e-872b-7a4c35796673")
	)
